# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL is not hardcoded anywhere in code (lib/api/config.ts) — it comes
# entirely from env files, which Expo loads in this order (later overrides earlier):
#   1. .env        — committed, shared default (localhost — safe, not a secret)
#   2. .env.local   — gitignored, your personal override (e.g. your LAN IP for a physical
#                      device or Android Emulator)
#
# This file is just a template/reference; edit .env or .env.local directly, not this one.
#
# The right value depends on how you're running the app:
#   - iOS Simulator / web:           http://127.0.0.1:8000
#   - Android Emulator:              http://10.0.2.2:8000   (127.0.0.1 means the emulator itself)
#   - Expo Go on a physical device:  http://<your-machine-LAN-IP>:8000
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
